  "description": "6851 Sycamore - Clear basal and epicormic growth, and remove deadwood.\r6850 Common Ash - Create pollard structure at 2m away from crown break back to closest growth points and sever ivy at base.\r6849 Sycamore - Crown reduce, sever ivy to 2m, remove leaning secondary stem (no herbicide), and clear deadwood in canopy.\r6848 Cherry Laurel - Pollard to approximately 2.4m above ground level; wounds will exceed 10cm but species is tolerant.\r6847 Common Ash - Fell to 50cm above ground and treat with systemic herbicide.\r6846 Apple Species - Fell to approximately 1m above ground and treat with systemic herbicide.\r6845 Sycamore - Crown reduce, sever ivy to 2m, cut ivy back to stem in canopy to allow for full inspection, remove deadwood, remove lowest limb on South Western aspect (approx 3.5m) back to stem and crown lift to 4m above ground level.\r6844 Common Holly - Fell to 50cm above ground and treat with systemic herbicide.\r6843 Horse Chestnut - Clear basal and epicormic growth and sever ivy to 2m above ground.\r6842 Sycamore - Re-coppice stems back to ground level.\r6841 Pedunculate Oak - Crown reduce, sever ivy to 2m, cut ivy in canopy for inspection, and remove deadwood.\r",
